# GHAFRA Backend

The GHAFRA API is an Express and TypeScript service backed by Supabase. It
also integrates Firebase Cloud Messaging, Resend, Stripe, Groq, and Hugging
Face.

## Requirements

- Node.js 20+
- npm
- A configured Supabase project and the external service credentials listed in
  `.env.example`

## Local setup

```bash
cd backend
cp .env.example .env
# Fill in every value in .env. Never commit .env or service credentials.
npm ci
npm run dev
```

The API listens on `PORT` (5000 by default). Check it with
`http://localhost:5000/health`.

## Commands

```bash
npm run dev       # watch mode
npm run build     # type-check and create dist/
npm start         # run the compiled service
npm test          # run the test suite (no network; Supabase is faked)
npm run db:migrate
npm run db:seed
```

`npm ci` installs the versions already recorded in `package-lock.json`; it
does not add dependencies to the project.

## Environment

`.env.example` documents all variables validated by `src/config/env.ts`.
Server-only keys must stay in the backend environment and must never be
copied into a browser or mobile `.env` file.

